# Rule machinery: the files that define and check this repository's rules.
# By team convention, a core developer other than the author approves changes
# to them (api.process.rule-machinery-code-owned). GitHub doesn't enforce
# this: the default branch's ruleset needs one approving review from anyone
# with write access and doesn't require code-owner review. Listing a path here
# only makes GitHub request a review from its owners on pull requests that
# change it and aren't drafts.
# Deliberately narrow: pyproject.toml and workflow files are not listed, so
# dependency bots and everyday CI edits don't request that review.
/rules/                         @PolicyEngine/core-developers
/scripts/rules/                 @PolicyEngine/core-developers
/scripts/guards/                @PolicyEngine/core-developers
/scripts/run_quality_guards.py  @PolicyEngine/core-developers
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @PolicyEngine/core-developers
